          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-8-ss-3-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6ec3af821def941fc1767039f23e419048b2288b6f741e4550d8d047944dac9a",
      "skos:note": "Disclosure of information by a corporation is permitted under certain conditions. A corporation may be taken to have made a disclosure of information for the purpose of substantially lessening competition in a market."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-act#sch-1-sec-8-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "8(3) Competition and Consumer Amendment Act (No. 1) 2011       No. 185, 2011",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 12,
      "values:originalText": "(3) Without limiting the manner in which the purpose of a person may\nbe established for the purposes of any other provision of this Act, a\ncorporation may be taken to have made a disclosure of information\nfor the purpose of substantially lessening competition in a market\neven though, after all the evidence has been considered, the\nexistence of that purpose is ascertainable only by inference from\nthe conduct of the corporation or of any other person or from other\nrelevant circumstances.\n44ZZY  Exceptions that apply to sections 44ZZW and 44ZZX\nDisclosure authorised by law: general exception for 10 years"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-8-ss-3-norm",
